		(property "Design Note" "3V3A rail monitor divider, 1:2 into MCU PA7/ADC_IN7. FIRMWARE: VA_MON_MV = 2 x ADC. This IS the sourcing pass the old note asked for. The position was 0.1% 10k (P2TC0603D1002LNTA) only because R21/R22 once shared it, and those went with the trim and guard dividers. Nothing downstream SCALES by this reading -- it is rail health. Contrast VREF_MON, whose ratio main.c promotes into g_cyc.vref_mv and thence into the reported cell current: R34/R35 stay 0.1% for exactly that reason and this pair does not need to. 47k rather than 10k also drops the continuous draw on the analog rail feeding U4/U7/U8 from 165 uA to 35 uA. Source impedance goes 5k -> 23.5k, and that is CHECKED, not assumed: ST DS12232 Table 59 (Maximum ADC RAIN) allows 50k at 12 bits and 160.5 sampling cycles, which is what mcu_adc.c already selects -- 2.1x margin, and more in practice because Table 59 is quoted at a 35 MHz ADC clock where this board runs 16 MHz. DO NOT RAISE THIS DIVIDER FURTHER: 100k legs would put the source at exactly the 50k limit. It releases the matched-pair placement adjacency the two-layer refloorplan work was holding"
			(at 0 0 90)
			(layer "B.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "98d88b89-a185-53bd-bf6a-cabea4336566")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
				(justify mirror)
			)
		)
